course: dictionary
lesson: 5666
title: One word, four meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word litter is a good example. «Camping means living outdoors for a while, so you choose a safe place for the tent, keep the camp clean, and leave no litter behind.» Leave no litter behind means do not leave rubbish, so litter is rubbish.
explain: «A frog from Papua New Guinea about seven millimetres long is one of the smallest animals with a backbone, living in leaf litter and eating tiny insects.» Could leaf litter be rubbish? Try it: a frog living in rubbish does not make sense here. Leaf litter is the dead leaves and bits lying on the ground in a wood, so the context clue is the word leaf.
explain: «Sam spoke up in assembly about the litter in the park.» He is talking about rubbish, because the park is a public place. «Plastic, once a wonder, now litters beaches» uses litters as a verb: plastic is spread over the beaches as rubbish. Always ask: what meaning fits this sentence?
fact: Litter can mean rubbish, like paper, cans and wrappers, left lying on the ground in a public place.
fact: A litter is a group of baby animals born to one mother at the same time, as in «a litter of puppies».
fact: Cat litter is the material in a tray that a cat uses as a toilet, so wash your hands after you change it.
fact: To litter means to drop rubbish on the ground, or to be spread untidily over a place.
fact: Put your rubbish in a bin or take it home, because litter can harm wildlife when animals get trapped in it or eat it.
exercise: «Camping means living outdoors for a while, so you choose a safe place for the tent, keep the camp clean, and leave no litter behind.» What does litter mean here? | To spread rubbish over a place | * Rubbish left lying around | Animals born at the same time | The material a cat uses in its tray
exercise: «A frog ... living in leaf litter and eating tiny insects.» What is leaf litter? | * Dead leaves and bits lying on the ground | Plastic wrappers blown into the trees | A group of baby frogs
exercise: Mum says, «Wash your hands after you change the cat litter.» What is cat litter? | * The material in a tray that a cat uses as a toilet | A group of kittens born together | A type of cat food | A bin for rubbish in the park
test: «Plastic, once a wonder, now litters beaches.» What does litters mean in this sentence? | * To spread rubbish untidily over the beaches | To clean the sand carefully | To make a tray for a cat | To count baby animals
test: «A litter of puppies» means what? | A walk in the park with dogs | * A group of baby puppies born to one mother at the same time | A tray for the puppies to use | A bin full of rubbish
exam: In «a litter of puppies», which meaning of litter fits? | Cat material in a tray | Rubbish on the ground | * A group of baby animals born to one mother at the same time | To drop rubbish on the ground
